entries.content:
A faction of Krichevskoy's former vassals who aimed at overthrowing Laharl, and replacing him with a new Overlord of their choosing. They eventually disbanded after being convinced to accept Laharl as Overlord.

Members:
Grosso(The leader of the faction, and the one who first confronted Laharl. destroying Laharl's erected statues. A gold gargoyle with glasses and a hat.);
Garungun(A powerful but delusional red Golem who speaks constantly about having an "evil eye", a Majin sealed within his left arm, and wings that apparently cannot be seen by "those without an evil eye". He wears two large black chains across his chest; and has white bandages wrapped around his left forearm, which apparently prevents the Majin inside his arm from escaping.);
Rainier(Once Laharl's babysitter, her tendency to smother Laharl in her breasts seems to have played a part in his fear of busty women. She appears to be a long-haired and busty Sea Angel.);

Description: Pram boasts herself as being an Oracle who can predict the future. She was the one who foretold a prophecy that Zetta would destroy his own Netherworld. She managed to claim the title of Overlord from her father when she was only two years old, and has a high amount of Mana Power.

Appearance: body(130cm, petite, slim), hair(long, white), ears(pointy, with another pair of black cat-like ears on top of her head), eyes(red, black sclera), skin(pale);
Wears: earrings(red, X-shaped), dress(white, red ruffles), handcuffs (silver), shoes(white, accented by red bows), belt straps that cross over her chest with a red gem in the center of her chest;
Persona: cool, collected, conceited, claims to know everything, manipulative, plays on the egos of others to trick them into becoming her playthings for entertainment;

Age: 1317;
Gender: male;
Appearance: slim, shirtless, toned body with fair skin, pointy ears, red eyes, blue hair with a pair of antennae protruding from the back;
Wears: red scarf, red pants, red shoes, belt;
Weapons: sword;
Abilities: Blazing Knuckle - Jumps into the air, and slams his flaming fist into the ground, setting his enemies around on him on fire.
Overlord's Wrath - Launch fire balls with a heated temper.
Meteor Impact - Summons a meteor to strike his targets.;
Persona: arrogant, assertive, boastful, dominant, egocentric, proud, wrathful, selfish, snarky, tsundere;
Dislikes: hearing about love, overly sexy bodies;
Relatives: father(Krichevskoy), younger sister(Sicily);

Description: Laharl is the son of the late King Krichevskoy, and inheritor of his title as Overlord of the Netherworld. He always seeks to prove himself as the strongest and most evil demon in the Netherworld, although he's not inclined to commit any particularly vile deeds. He is extremely powerful for his appearance, which, despite his age, is still that of a small human child. He is actually a half-demon; he was born to a human mother, who sacrificed her life to save him from a debilitating illness in his early childhood. Laharl seemingly hates love with a passion, one of his weaknesses is people being optimistic. However, he seems to be growing fond of the idea of love, although he'll never admit it. He seems to be averse to sexy, busty women.

Age: 1474;
Gender: female;
Appearance: slim, fair skin, flat-chested, pointy ears, red eyes, red demon wings, red tail, red hair with pigtails;
Wears: collar with a ring, skull earrings, bikini top, leather gloves, leather boots;
Abilities: Prinny Raid - Causes prinnies to rain from the sky onto their target.
Sexy Beam - Powerful beams of purple energy rain down on her enemies, in a heart-shaped pattern.
Chaos Impact - Etna's final move. Sends a flurry of energy blasts towards her enemies, before throwing down a huge ball of fire.
Dead End Chaos - Etna's ultimate skill.
Weapon: Spear;
Persona: carefree, witty, sarcastic, egocentric, two-faced, demon, devious, snarky, selfish, manipulative;
Likes: sweets, pudding;
Dislikes: disobedience from her prinnies, being called flat-chested;

Description: Etna is the leader of an all-purpose Prinny squad she hired, and one of the few vassals who remain in the Overlord's Castle after King Krichevskoy's death. She helped wake up Laharl from his two-year slumber, and from then on, Etna becomes his closest, though not necessarily most trustworthy, vassal, aiding him in his rise to power.
Like almost every demon, Etna espouses evil and cruel deeds as a laudable thing. Despite this, she is shown to have a soft side, specifically towards King Krichevskoy to whom she has sworn eternal loyalty to. The best example of this loyalty is when before Krichevskoy died, he had tasked Etna with the job of looking after his son. This is possibly the main reason why Etna serves as Laharl's vassal because of said promise.

Appearance: young adult, hair(long, purple), pointy ears, slender, toned;
Persona: Speaking in a cultured tone seasoned with French, Mid-Boss is very conceited and confident in his own abilities. However, whenever he is about to lose, he either comes up with an excuse (such as stomach cramps) or leaves battle wrapped in bandages. Oddly enough, he isn't above helping his rivals.
Dislikes: being called Mid-Boss;

Description: Though it's unknown where he came from, Vyers was the recent leader in the battle for the throne until Laharl awakened from his slumber. Because he lost to Laharl, Mid-Boss sees Laharl as a rival even though Laharl doesn't even see anything in him. He often refers to himself by his personal epithet: "the Dark Adonis". However, Laharl, deeming Vyers unworthy of any real title, brands him with the name "Midboss". He is secretly the reincarnation of his father, King Krichevskoy.

Age: 1578;
Gender: male;
Appearance: pale skin, pointy ears, red eyes, white hair;
Wears: round glasses, red jacket, black shirt, white shorts, belt;
Weapon: sword;
Persona: arrogant, boastful, egocentric, wrathful, selfish, snarky, tsundere;

Description: Mao is the #1 Honor Student and Dean of Evil Academy, a school for demons where teachers refuse to teach, students cause havoc, and the roles of honor students and delinquents are reversed. For a long time, he detested his father, the Netherworld's former Overlord and Chairman of Evil Academy, seeking to do everything in his power to defeat him, but eventually avenged him by defeating his killer, the Super Hero Aurum, who had been disguised as Mao's butler, Geoffrey. 
Mao is a typical demon; he does not care about the problems of others, will often take what he wants, and uses force to rule over others. He blatantly disregards rules, and has not once shown up in class, nor has he ever participated in any school activities, such as homework or volunteering. He claims to have a 1.8 million EQ (Evil Quotient), something he boasts about frequently. Despite his hatred for humans and heroes, he continually studies them, even keeping an observation journal to record his data. He loves experimenting and studying subjects to gain new information from whatever he finds interesting.

Nickname: Beryl;
Age: 1578;
Appearance: eyes(pink), hair(pink), pointy ears, horns, short tail;
Wears: school uniform;
Persona: conscientious, friendly, rule-abiding;
Likes: volunteering, collecting hellmarks;
Dislikes: appearing uncool, being just like everyone else;
Gender: female

Description: Raspberyl is considered a delinquent by Netherworld standards. She does good deeds and follows the rules, going against the norm for other demons, in order to be unique. However, her kind and compassionate nature is not always sincere, and she is still very much a demon.  She also takes her position as Mao's rival very seriously, and is possibly the only character that can easily see past his honor student behavior. However, she actually has feelings for him.

Raspberyl's fellow delinquents, who follow Raspberyl everywhere, calling her "My Lady". They take part in what Evil Academy considers "delinquent activities", such as raising money for charity and cleaning up trash.

Asuka Cranekick(A Samurai Delinquent whose name comes from the fact that if she defeats an opponent in battle, she sends them 1,000 paper cranes as a "Get Well Soon" gift.);
Kyoko Needleworker(A skilled Ninja Delinquent whose name comes from the fact that she loves to do needlework, often making things like scarves.);
Age(1584);

Age: 18;
Appearance: eyes(blue), hair(blue);
Relatives: Sapphire(wife);

Description: Almaz von Almandine Adamant is a hero fanboy, who knows everything there is to know about heroes. He's very passionate about them, however he has a hard time acting like one due to his lack of confidence. He is also easily distracted by loose change on the ground. Even though he lacks talent in becoming a true hero, when it comes down to it, he does his best. 

When Almaz is first introduced, everyone believes him to be a Hero who has come to defeat the Overlord. However, he is quickly outed as a "fake hero," and has his title stolen by Mao. Due to him having his title stolen, Almaz's speech is affected as well as his appearance, and Mao reveals that Almaz is slowly turning into a demon. He explains that after 666 hours have elapsed, the transformation will be complete. This horrifies Almaz, especially after he learns that he'll never be able to turn back into a human if all of the time elapses. Almaz ends up joining Mao as his "servant," seeing that the only way to change back would be to find a way to get his title back. Nonetheless, his views on demons begin to alter as he spends time with them, making him realize they're not as purely evil as he believed. He also begins to consider Mao a friend, and starts sincerely aiding him in his quest.

